.TH MONKEY-WSL2 1 "2026-08-30" "realisateur" "migration runbook"
.SH NAME
monkey-wsl2 \- move monkey from a VirtualBox guest to a WSL2 distro on dexter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
./etat.sh                                   where this actually is, probed live
./constate.sh > before.tsv                  the baseline witness
./constate.sh --target wsl:monkey --diff before.tsv    the verdict, after
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Executable form of the decision in hf7y/senechal#438: monkey stops being a
VirtualBox guest and becomes a WSL2 distro on dexter, and VirtualBox leaves
entirely. dexter's Hyper-V holds AMD-V, so VirtualBox falls back to NEM and
monkey is descheduled for seconds at a time; 14.5h wedged in 42h. One
hypervisor means no contention.
.PP
Run
.B ./etat.sh
first. It re-derives every step from hosts and repos rather than reading a box
a human ticked.
.PP
.B THE ORDER BELOW IS PROVISIONAL.
The rehearsal exists to change it. A step that diverges is a FINDING, not a
failure: record what was discovered here, amend the order, and re-run.
.SH ROUTES, AND WHICH SURVIVE WHAT
.nf
ssh monkey     the guest itself, tailnet 100.121.83.23
ssh dexter     port 2223 = dexter's WSL2 sshd, in the distro named `Ubuntu'
ssh \-p 22 \-i ~/.ssh/id_dexter_win zach@dexter.tail893f2c.ts.net
               Windows sshd, PowerShell 5.1, High Mandatory Level Administrator
.fi
.PP
.B wsl \-\-shutdown
and
.B wsl \-\-import
kill the 2223 route mid\-procedure. Only the Windows route survives them, so it
drives every step that restarts WSL.
.B wsl \-\-terminate <one>
is safe.
.PP
.B \-\-shutdown IS NOT. ITS BLAST RADIUS IS THE ESTATE'S CHANNEL TO ZACH.
It stops EVERY distro. Measured on hermes 2026\-08\-30 (hf7y/senechal#557):
.nf

  zaxon\-relay\-mcp.service      ask_zach / check_zach_reply
  zaxon\-relay\-watcher.service  the WhatsApp reply watcher
  whisper\-server.service       STT, port 8090
  hermes\-gateway.service       messaging platform integration
.fi
.PP
plus dexter's own sshd on 2223 and the monkey\-watch.sh crontab living in it. So
.B \-\-shutdown
takes Zach's own notification channel dark at the same moment it removes the
route you would use to put it back. Never run it from the 2223 route, and
prefer terminating one distro by name.
.PP
.B hermes IS NOT UNUSED.
senechal#438's revision quotes "hermes is unused, shared kernel is fine" \- that
is a premise, not a measurement, and #557 disproved it. Anything treating
hermes as disposable needs re\-deriving. The distros share one WSL2 network
namespace, so a port check run from `Ubuntu' actually measures hermes and
cannot say so: distro identity is not observable from inside a distro here.
.PP
dexter reaches monkey directly, so 27G never crosses mandark. Run ON dexter:
.nf

  ssh \-n \-i ~/.ssh/id_dexter_monkey zach@100.121.83.23 'hostname'
.fi
.SH FACTS THAT CHANGE THE COMMANDS
.nf
C:  53G free   monkey.vdi is 39.5G and lives HERE \- rollback depends on it
D:  2.6T free  every large write goes here, never to C:
monkey.vbox is on D: while monkey.vdi is on C: \- the VM is split across drives
distros: docker\-desktop (DEFAULT), Ubuntu, hermes \- and hermes is NOT spare:
  it holds ask_zach, the WhatsApp watcher and whisper (senechal#557)
ALL distros share ONE network namespace, net:[4026531833] \- measured, identical
  inode from Ubuntu and hermes. So a distro's ports are the estate's ports.
  taken: 2223 8643 8090 3000 8642 53. FREE: 22, which is what monkey binds.
  a bare `wsl \-d' with no name hits docker\-desktop, not yours
Ubuntu and hermes BOTH report hostname `dexter'; /etc/wsl.conf is per\-distro
monkey guest: systemd\-networkd and systemd\-resolved ACTIVE, / mounted by UUID,
  /swapfile in fstab \- all break or hang under wsl \-\-import
.fi
.SS Why a probe here cannot identify what it measured
One namespace, and two distros answering to the same hostname, means
.B a check run inside a distro cannot tell you which distro it measured.
Three separate confusions on 2026\-08\-30 were this one fact:
.nf

  a port check from `Ubuntu' reports hermes's 8643 and 8090 as its own \-
    which is why dexter\-liveness.sh calls hermes dead weight while
    declaring the very ports hermes owns
  `wsl.exe \-e true' warns about a wsl.conf key belonging to docker\-desktop,
    because with no \-d it launches the DEFAULT distro, not yours
  `ssh dexter' and `wsl \-d hermes' both answer the hostname `dexter'
.fi
.PP
So: name the distro explicitly in every command, and treat any measurement that
did not name one as unattributed rather than as belonging to the caller.
.SH WHERE THE SEQUENCE HAS GOT TO
.nf
2026\-08\-30  seam merged (#745, #798); wsl arms for disk/screenshot/logdir added
2026\-08\-30  before.tsv captured: backend=oracle, 12/12 runners, node
            nyzii8E1C221CNTRL, long_readout=4, soft_lockup=1
            NOT yet run: rehearsal, cutover
.fi
.SH 0. BASELINE, BEFORE ANYTHING TOUCHES MONKEY
.nf

  ./constate.sh > before.tsv && cat before.tsv
.fi
.SH 1. REHEARSAL \- A THROWAWAY COPY; MONKEY KEEPS RUNNING
Answers by measurement what no issue currently knows: whether systemd comes up,
whether the 12 runner units start, and whether tailscaled works inside a distro
under networkingMode=mirrored. Nothing here touches monkey. About 27G, 5 min.
.PP
ON dexter (route: ssh dexter):
.nf

  # the distros share ONE netns, so check for a collision BEFORE importing:
  # monkey listens on nothing hermes uses today, but 8643 and 8090 are taken.
  wsl.exe \-d hermes \-u root \-\- ss \-ltn | awk 'NR>1{print $4}' | sort \-u

  mkdir \-p /mnt/d/wsl\-migration
  ssh \-n \-i ~/.ssh/id_dexter_monkey zach@100.121.83.23 \e
\&    'sudo tar \-c \-\-numeric\-owner \-\-xattrs \-\-acls \-C / \e
\&       \-\-exclude=./proc \-\-exclude=./sys \-\-exclude=./dev \-\-exclude=./run \e
\&       \-\-exclude=./tmp \-\-exclude=./mnt \-\-exclude=./media \e
\&       \-\-exclude=./lost+found \-\-exclude=./swapfile \e
\&       \-\-exclude=./var/lib/tailscale/tailscaled.state .' \e
    > /mnt/d/wsl\-migration/monkey\-rehearsal.tar
.fi
.PP
tailscaled.state is dropped ON PURPOSE here: the rehearsal takes a FRESH
identity so monkey's own node is never at risk. The cutover keeps it.
.PP
ON dexter, Windows route. Imports land on D:, never C:
.nf

  wsl.exe \-\-import monkey\-rehearsal D:\ewsl\-migration\emonkey\-rehearsal \e
    D:\ewsl\-migration\emonkey\-rehearsal.tar
  wsl.exe \-d monkey\-rehearsal \-u root \-\- /bin/true
.fi
.SS The first boot is the safe window, and it is the only one
monkey carries no /etc/wsl.conf \- it has never been a distro \- so the FIRST
.B wsl \-d
boots WITHOUT systemd, because systemd=true is off by default. Nothing of
monkey's starts. That is the one window in which to disarm what must not run,
and it closes the moment section 2 writes a wsl.conf.
.PP
.B MASK THE RUNNERS BEFORE ANYTHING ELSE, OR THE REHEARSAL ATTACKS THE FLEET.
monkey has 12 enabled actions.runner units holding registered agent names
(monkey\-senechal, agentId 21, and eleven more). Under systemd they would
connect to GitHub as the SAME agents as the live monkey and contend for its
jobs. The rehearsal is meant to cost nothing; this is how it would cost the
fleet instead.
.nf

  wsl.exe \-d monkey\-rehearsal \-u root \-\- \e
    systemctl mask 'actions.runner.*' tailscaled cron
.fi
.PP
tailscaled and cron are masked for the same reason: the rehearsal must not
reach the tailnet or fire monkey's crontabs. Only then apply section 2's fixes,
restart, and record what actually happened:
.nf

  wsl.exe \-\-terminate monkey\-rehearsal
  wsl.exe \-d monkey\-rehearsal \-u root \-\- systemctl is\-system\-running
  wsl.exe \-d monkey\-rehearsal \-u root \-\- systemctl list\-units \-\-state=active
  wsl.exe \-d monkey\-rehearsal \-u root \-\- systemctl is\-enabled tailscaled
  wsl.exe \-d monkey\-rehearsal \-u root \-\- tailscale \-\-version
.fi
.PP
The tailscale question the rehearsal exists to answer is whether tailscaled can
run inside a distro at all under networkingMode=mirrored \- not whether it can
take monkey's identity. Test it with a FRESH auth key against a throwaway node
name, never with monkey's state. dexter's own tailscaled runs on WINDOWS,
OUTSIDE WSL, so it proves nothing about this.
.PP
Write the answers to rehearsal\-verdict.tsv, then tear it down:
.nf

  wsl.exe \-\-unregister monkey\-rehearsal
  rm \-f /mnt/d/wsl\-migration/monkey\-rehearsal.tar
.fi
.SH 2. GUEST PREP \- WHAT MAKES AN IMPORTED ROOT ACTUALLY BOOT
Apply INSIDE the imported distro, never on the live guest, so a failed import
costs nothing.
.nf

  # / is mounted by UUID and no such device exists in WSL2; /swapfile likewise
  sed \-i 's|^/dev/disk/by\-uuid|#&|; s|^/swapfile|#&|' /etc/fstab

  # WSL2 writes /etc/resolv.conf and owns the interface; these fight it for DNS
  systemctl mask systemd\-networkd systemd\-resolved multipathd lvm2\-monitor \e
    ModemManager

  cat > /etc/wsl.conf <<'EOF'
  [boot]
  systemd=true
  [user]
  default=zach
  [network]
  hostname=monkey
  EOF
.fi
.PP
hostname=monkey matters: Ubuntu and hermes BOTH answer `dexter', and a third
distro answering `dexter' makes every host\-keyed probe ambiguous.
.SH 3. CUTOVER
Only after the rehearsal has a recorded verdict.
.nf

  ssh monkey 'sudo systemctl stop "actions.runner.*"'   # quiesce, do NOT deregister
  ./constate.sh > before\-cutover.tsv
.fi
.PP
ON dexter. The same tar as section 1 but KEEPING tailscaled.state \- that state
is what makes `Host monkey' and 12 runner registrations keep resolving.
.nf

  ssh \-n \-i ~/.ssh/id_dexter_monkey zach@100.121.83.23 \e
\&    'sudo tar \-c \-\-numeric\-owner \-\-xattrs \-\-acls \-C / \e
\&       \-\-exclude=./proc \-\-exclude=./sys \-\-exclude=./dev \-\-exclude=./run \e
\&       \-\-exclude=./tmp \-\-exclude=./mnt \-\-exclude=./media \e
\&       \-\-exclude=./lost+found \-\-exclude=./swapfile .' \e
    > /mnt/d/wsl\-migration/monkey.tar
.fi
.PP
Windows route. The VM is SAVED, never deleted \- that is the rollback.
.nf

  & 'C:\eProgram Files\eOracle\eVirtualBox\eVBoxManage.exe' controlvm monkey savestate
  wsl.exe \-\-import monkey D:\ewsl\-migration\emonkey D:\ewsl\-migration\emonkey.tar
  wsl.exe \-d monkey \-u root \-\- /bin/true
.fi
.PP
Apply section 2 inside it, then verify BEFORE trusting it:
.nf

  ./constate.sh \-\-target wsl:monkey \-\-diff before.tsv
.fi
.PP
Every MUST\-HOLD field must hold and backend must FLIP oracle \-> wsl. A MOVED
machine_id or an ABSENT ts_nodeid means STOP and roll back.
.SH ROLLBACK
Reversible at every step because the VDI is never touched.
.nf

  wsl.exe \-\-terminate monkey
  wsl.exe \-\-unregister monkey
  & 'C:\eProgram Files\eOracle\eVirtualBox\eVBoxManage.exe' startvm monkey \-\-type headless
  ./constate.sh \-\-diff before.tsv
.fi
.PP
Expect backend back to oracle and every field held.
.SH THE TWO GATES ONLY ZACH CAN PASS
Neither blocks the rehearsal. The second blocks only runner re\-registration,
and selfdev\-runner\-provision.sh retries daily, so it is recoverable after the
fact rather than a stop.
.nf

HUMAN\-STEP
  what:     approve the forced verb\-build cut so fixed host tools reach dexter
  where:    github.com/hf7y/verbs \-> Actions \-> build\-verbs \-> the waiting run
  verified: gh api repos/hf7y/verbs/environments shows release with
            required_reviewers [hf7y] and can_admins_bypass false, so a
            workflow_dispatch run starts and then waits rather than failing
  undo:     cancel the queued run; the 30\-day cadence is unchanged either way

HUMAN\-STEP
  what:     grant the GitHub App Administration: read & write (senechal#551)
  where:    github.com/settings/installations \-> installation 152065281
  verified: the nightly registration\-token POST returns Not Found today, and
            no REST endpoint exists to grant this \- checked against the
            installation's current permission set
  undo:     revoke the same permission in the same UI
.fi
.SH WHAT A GOOD RUN PRODUCES
.nf

  HOLD  machine_id 25cb8cab...     FLIP backend oracle \-> wsl
  HOLD  ts_nodeid nyzii8E1C221CNTRL
  OK    runners_active 12 (was 12)
  OK    long_readout 0 (was 4)
.fi
.PP
A Long readout count that does NOT fall to 0 means monkey is still being
descheduled, and the migration did not buy what it was for.
.SH RETIRING THIS
When etat.sh reports the cutover DONE and a week has passed with long_readout
at 0, delete this directory, the saved VM, and D:\ewsl\-migration. Fold the
durable facts into bin/lib/vmhost.sh comments; leave nothing here to rot.
.SH IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
constate.sh and etat.sh carry no comments on purpose: their reasoning is here,
in one document, rather than scattered across two scripts.
.PP
.B constate.sh
runs on mandark and reaches in. It is NOT a verb and is installed on no host,
so it needs no build tag to reach the thing it measures \- which matters,
because the verb build cuts only every 30 days. Its probe is one heredoc run
wherever \-\-target says. Every field exists because something downstream breaks
when it moves:
.nf

  MUST\-HOLD    machine_id hostname accounts crontabs etc_selfdev verbs_on_path
               and ts_ip / ts_nodeid \- what `Host monkey' and 12 runner
               registrations resolve through. ABSENT is expected on the
               rehearsal distro, which takes a fresh key on purpose; a SILENT
               change on the real cutover is the failure this exists to catch.
  MUST\-CHANGE  backend, oracle \-> wsl. The one field whose job is to flip.
  GRADED       runners_active may not fall; long_readout and soft_lockup may
               not rise.
.fi
.PP
A witness that cannot see exits 6 (BLIND) rather than reporting a clean, empty
pass \- "I could not look" reported as healthy is how ten days pass.
.PP
.B etat.sh
re\-derives the sprint's position from hosts and repos on every run; it reads no
box a human ticked. It always exits 0, so it can never redden CI or block a
turn. It checks the four vmhost wsl arms whose absence renders the published
status page permanently red, and it measures C: free against monkey.vdi \-
because rollback lives or dies on C: keeping that file.
